        <mxCell id="-a9pnOCAbg5-bltNy8Gf-61" parent="1" style="text;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="We upload a CSV file with raw data to the bucket raw-file-pipeline-nak76700 on S3.&#xa;&#xa;Each time a file is uploaded, a Lambda function is automatically triggered and processes the raw data by reformatting and cleaning it, and creates a new processed file in another S3 bucket: processed-file-pipeline-nak76700.&#xa;&#xa;An AWS Glue Crawler automatically scans the CSV file to detect the structure, then creates the schema (tables, columns, data types) in the AWS Glue Data Catalog.&#xa;&#xa;The AWS Glue Data Catalog, which acts as a centralized metadata store, records this schema as a table that will be used by a Glue ETL job.&#xa;&#xa;An AWS Glue job retrieves the data, transforms it, and loads the final version of the file into a new S3 bucket: final-file-pipeline-nak76700.&#xa;&#xa;Amazon QuickSight connects to the final dataset and presents the dashboard for data visualization." vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="250" width="591" x="209" y="520" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="-a9pnOCAbg5-bltNy8Gf-62" parent="1" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#1ba1e2;fontColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=none;" value="1" vertex="1">
